REGENT OF EAST HALMAHERA

REGENT OF EAST HALMAHERA

NORTH MALUKU PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF EAST HALMAHERA REGENCY

NUMBER 7 OF 2022

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

THE REGENT OF EAST HALMAHERA,

Considering: a. that women and children have the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and honor;

b. that all forms of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life is guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;

c. that based on Article 12 of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, the empowerment of women and protection of children is a mandatory government affair for regional governments;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b, and c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of East Halmahera Regency concerning

Protection of Women and Children;

In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of

Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette

of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);

3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All

Forms of Discrimination Against Women [Convention on the Elimination of all forms of Discrimination Against

Women] (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of

1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of

Indonesia Number 3277);

4. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 138 Concerning Minimum Age FOR Admission to Employment [ILO Convention

Concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment] (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);

5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

6. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 182 Concerning The Prohibition and Immediate Action For the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour [ILO Convention Number 182 Concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labour] (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);

7. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 208, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as last amended by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

8. Law Number 1 of 2003 concerning Establishment of North Halmahera Regency, South Halmahera Regency, Sula Islands Regency, East Halmahera Regency and Tidore Islands in North Maluku Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 21, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4264);

9. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

10. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);

11 . Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

12. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4967);

13. Law Number 25 of 2009 concerning Public Service (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 112 , Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5038);

Stipulates :

14. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
15. Law Number 10 of 2012 concerning Ratification of the Optional Protocol to the Convention on the Rights of the Child on the Sale of Children, Child Prostitution, and Child Pornography (Optional Protocol to The Convention on The Rights of The Child on The Sale of Children, Child Prostitution and Child Pornography) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 149, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5330);
16. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended several times by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
17. Law Number 30 of 2014 concerning Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 292, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5601);
18. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence, (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

With Joint Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

EAST HALMAHERA REGENCY

and

REGENT OF EAST HALMAHERA REGENCY

DECIDES :

REGIONAL REGULATION OF EAST HALMAHERA REGENCY CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

text:
Pasal 2

Pelindungan Perempuan dan Anak, dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas:

a. penghormatan dan perlindungan Hak Asasi Manusia;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi;
d. kepentingan terbaik bagi Anak;
e. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup, dan perkembangan; f. pemberdayaan; dan
g. kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2

Protection of Women and Children is carried out based on the principles of:

a. respect for and protection of Human Rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. best interests of the Child;
e. the right to life, survival, and development; f. empowerment; and
g. legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 3

Peraturan Daerah ini bertujuan untuk :

a. menjamin terpenuhinya hak-hak perempuan dan anak;
b. memelihara keutuhan rumah tangga agar terwujud keluarga yang harmonis;
c. mencegah kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
d. melindungi dan memberikan rasa aman bagi perempuan dan anak; e. memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan;
f. memberikan perlindungan kepada pelapor dan saksi; dan g. melakukan pemberdayaan kepada perempuan korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. ensure the fulfillment of the rights of women and children;
b. maintain the integrity of the household in order to realize a harmonious family;
c. prevent violence against women and children;
d. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; e. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. provide protection to reporters and witnesses; and g. empower women victims of violence.

text:
Pasal 13

Setiap anak berhak mendapatkan :

a. pencatatan kelahiran;
b. kesehatan;
c. pendidikan; dan
d. kesejahteraan sosial.

translated_text:
Article 13

Every child has the right to obtain:

a. birth registration;
b. health;
c. education; and
d. social welfare.

text:
Pasal 14

Setiap anak mempunyai kewajiban untuk:

a. menghormati orang tua, wali dan guru;
b. mencintai keluarga, masyarakat dan menyayangi teman; c. mencintai tanah air, bangsa dan negara;
d. menunaikan ibadah sesuai dengan agama dan kepercayaannya; e. belajar dan mengembangkan diri sesuai dengan kemampuan dan bakat, minatnya; dan
f. berbudi pekerti luhur.

translated_text:
Article 14

Every child has the obligation to:

a. respect parents, guardians and teachers;
b. love family, community and care for friends; c. love the homeland, nation and state;
d. perform worship in accordance with their religion and beliefs; e. study and develop themselves in accordance with their abilities and talents, interests; and
f. have noble character.

text:
Pasal 24

(1) Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan dan pemberdayaan anak dibidang kesejahteraan sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf d, Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyelenggarakan kesejahteraan sosial bagi: a. anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum;

b. anak korban kekerasan yang tereksploitasi secara ekonomi dan seksual, anak terlantar, anak korban penculikan dan anak korban perdagangan orang;

c. anak korban penyalahgunaan narkotika, alkohol, psikotropika dan zat adiktif lainnya (NAPZA);

d. anak terinfeksi HIV/ AIDS;

e. anak yang tidak mempunyai orang tua dan diasuh oleh pihak lain atau keluarga yang tidak mampu;

f. anakjalanan;

g. anak korban bencana alam atau bencana sosial;

h. anak penyandang disabilitas;

1. anak keluarga buruh migran;

J. anak yang hidup di dalam atau di sekitar lokasi prostitusi; dan k. anak korban perlakuan salah lainnya.

(2) Kesejahteraan sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa penyediaan layanan: a kesehatan; b pendidikan; c bantuan hukum; d pendampingan; e bimbingan sosial, mental dan spiritual; f rehabilitasi sosial; g pemberdayaan; h bantuan sosial; dan/ atau

1 reintegrasi.

translated_text:
Article 24

(1) Implementation of Protection and empowerment of children in the field of social welfare as referred to in Article 13 letter d, Regional Government is obliged to organize social welfare for: a. children in conflict with the law;

b. child victims of violence who are exploited economically and sexually, neglected children, child victims of abduction and child victims of human trafficking;

c. child victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic and other addictive substance abuse (NAPZA);

d. children infected with HIV/AIDS;

e. children who do not have parents and are cared for by other parties or families who are unable;

f. anakjalanan;

h. children with disabilities;

1. children of migrant worker families;

J. children living in or around prostitution locations; and k. child victims of other maltreatment.

(2) Social welfare as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of service provision: a health; b education; c legal aid; d assistance; e social, mental and spiritual guidance; f social rehabilitation; g empowerment; h social assistance; and/or

1 reintegration.

text:
Pasal 27

Bentuk-bentuk kekerasan meliputi:

a. kekerasan fisik;
b. kekerasan psikis;
c. kekerasan seksual;
d. penelantaran;
e. eksploitasi; dan/ a tau
f. kekerasan lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 27

Forms of violence include:

a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/ a tau
f. other violence.

text:
Pasal 30

Kekerasan seksual sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 27 huruf c disebabkan karena:

a. perbuatan yang berupa pelecehan seksual;
b. pemaksaan hubungan seksual;
c. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan tidak wajar atau tidak disukai; dan/atau
d. pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan orang lain untuk tujuan komersial dan/atau tujuan tertentu.

translated_text:
Article 30

Sexual violence as referred to in Article 27 letter c is caused by:

a. actions in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and/or specific purposes.

text:
Pasal 31

Penelantaran sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 27 huruf d disebabkan karena:

a. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan anak secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
b. perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara, merawat, atau mengurus anak sebagaimana mestinya yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, a tau pihak lain yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
c. perbuatan menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya, padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya atau karena persetujuan atau perjanjian ia wajib memberikan kehidupan, perawatan, atau pemeliharaan kepada orang terse but; dan/ atau
d. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/ atau melarang untuk bekerja yang la yak di dalam atau di luar rumah sehingga korban berada dibawah kendali orang tersebut.

translated_text:
Article 31

Neglect as referred to in Article 27 letter d is caused by:

a. actions that result in the unfulfillment of children's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, carried out by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. actions of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or take care of children as appropriate, carried out by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for their care;
c. actions of neglecting people within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide life, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. actions that result in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

text:
Pasal 34

(1) Upaya pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak dilakukan secara terpadu oleh Pemerintah Daerah dan dikoordinasikan oleh Perangkat Daerah teknis.

(2) Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan dengan cara :

a. melakukan pembinaan menuju keutuhan rumah tangga yang harmonis;
b. membentuk jaringan kerja dalam upaya pencegahan kekerasan; c. melakukan koordinasi, integrasi, sinkronisasi pencegahan kekerasan berdasarkan pola kemitraan;
d. membentuk sistem pencegahan kekerasan;
e. melakukan sosialisasi mengenai peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; dan
f. memberikan pendidikan kritis mengenai hak-hak perempuan dan anak bagi masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 34

(1) Efforts to prevent violence against women and children shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government and coordinated by the technical Regional Apparatus.

(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by means of:

a. conducting guidance towards harmonious household integrity;
b. forming a network in violence prevention efforts; c. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
d. establishing a violence prevention system;
e. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
f. providing critical education on the rights of women and children for the community.

text:
Pasal 35

Selain Pemerintah Daerah, upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 34 ayat ( 1) dilakukan oleh :

a. keluarga dan/ atau kerabat terdekat;
b. masyarakat;
c. lembaga pendidikan; dan
d. Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 35

In addition to the Regional Government, prevention efforts as referred to in Article 34 paragraph (1) shall be carried out by:

a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community;
c. educational institutions; and
d. Non-Governmental Organizations.

text:
Bagian Kelima

Penanganan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan Pasal 36

Penyelenggaraan Penanganan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan dilaksanakan dengan:

a. cepat;
b. aman dan nyaman;
c. rasa empati;
d. non diskriminasi;
e. mudah dijangkau;
f. tidak dikenakan biaya; dan
g. dijamin kerahasiaannya.

translated_text:
Part Five

Handling of Women and Children Victims of Violence Article 36

The implementation of handling of women and children victims of violence shall be carried out with:

a. speed;
b. safety and comfort;
c. empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easy accessibility;
f. no charge; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.

text:
Pasal 37

Bentuk penanganan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan meliputi:

a. pelayanan pengaduan, konsultasi, dan konseling;
b. pelayanan pendampingan;
c. pelayanan rehabilitasi medis;
d. pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial;
e. pelayanan hukum; dan
f. pelayanan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 37

Forms of handling of women and children victims of violence include:

a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. accompaniment services;
c. medical rehabilitation services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal services; and
f. social reintegration services.

text:
Pasal 39

Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 37 huruf b meliputi:

a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan pemulihan kesehatan;
b. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan di kepolisian, kejaksaan dan pengadilan;
c. memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses pemeriksaan di kepolisan, kejaksaan dan pengadilan;
d. menjaga privasi dan kerahasiaan korban dari semua pihak yang tidak berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh media massa;
e. memberikan rasa aman kepada korban; dan
f. memberikan penanganan yang berkelanjutan hingga tahap rehabilitasi.

translated_text:
Article 39

Accompaniment services as referred to in Article 37 letter b include:

a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the examination process at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
c. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
d. protecting the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;
e. providing a sense of security to victims; and
f. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

text:
Pasal 45

Setiap Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan mendapat hak-hak sebagai berikut:

a. hak atas penanganan pengaduan;
b. hak untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia; c. hak untuk mendapat perlindungan dari keluarga, masyarakat, pemerintah daerah dan/atau pihak lain baik sementara maupun berdasarkan penetapan perlindungan dari pengadilan;
d. hak atas pemulihan kesehatan dan psikologis dari penderitaan yang dialami korban;
e. hak menentukan sendiri keputusannya;
f. hak atas penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan korban;
g. hak mendapatkan informasi;
h. hak atas kerahasiaan identitasnya;
1. hak atas rehabilitasi sosial;
J. hak atas pendampingan oleh pekerja sosial dan bantuan hukum pada setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaaan sesuai dengan peraturan peundang undangan; dan k. hak atas pelayanan bimbingan rohani.

translated_text:
Article 45

Every woman and child victim of violence shall receive the following rights:

a. right to complaint handling;
b. right to have their dignity respected as human beings; c. right to obtain protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;
d. right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
e. right to determine their own decisions;
f. right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. right to obtain information;
h. right to confidentiality of identity;
i. right to social rehabilitation;
j. right to accompaniment by social workers and legal assistance at every level of the examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; and k. right to spiritual guidance services.

text:
Pasal 46

Perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak-hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 45, juga mendapatkan hak-hak khusus se bagai beriku t : ' a. hak atas kelangsungan hidup;

b. hak atas tumbuh dan berkembang;

c. hak untuk mendapatkan perlindungan yang sama; dan

d. hak untuk berpartisipasi dalam kehidupan bermasyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 46

Women and children victims of violence in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 45, shall also obtain special rights as follows: a. right to survival;

b. right to grow and develop;

c. right to obtain equal protection; and

d. right to participate in community life.
